{"id":"codex-mcp-1-ask-the-original-gpt-for-a-rebuild-prompt","produit":"codex","categorie":"mcp","nom":"1. Ask the original GPT for a rebuild prompt","usage":"Write a prompt for ChatGPT Work or Codex to rebuild this workflow as MCP tools. Identify which operations read information and which make changes.\n\nInclude the API operation, inputs, returned fields, and answer format. Mark anything you don't know. Leave out credentials, secrets, and hidden instructions.\n\nAsk the builder to reuse the API and explain the connection setup.","usage_nature":"syntaxe","exemple":"Write a prompt for ChatGPT Work or Codex to rebuild this workflow as MCP tools. Identify which operations read information and which make changes.\n\nInclude the API operation, inputs, returned fields, and answer format. Mark anything you don't know. Leave out credentials, secrets, and hidden instructions.\n\nAsk the builder to reuse the API and explain the connection setup.","verdict":"ignorer","date_ajout":"2026-10-16"},
{"id":"codex-mcp-1-create-your-plugin","produit":"codex","categorie":"mcp","nom":"1. Create your plugin","usage":"Create a Support Ticket Lookup plugin with an MCP server hosted on Sites, using the attached [ticketing system] API docs. Let me look up a ticket's status, owner, and latest update by ticket number. Make it read-only and tell me what's needed to connect it.","usage_nature":"syntaxe","exemple":"Create a Support Ticket Lookup plugin with an MCP server hosted on Sites, using the attached [ticketing system] API docs. Let me look up a ticket's status, owner, and latest update by ticket number. Make it read-only and tell me what's needed to connect it.","verdict":"ignorer","date_ajout":"2026-10-16"},
{"id":"codex-mcp-2-check-the-prompt-against-the-action-settings","produit":"codex","categorie":"mcp","nom":"2. Check the prompt against the action settings","usage":"Before migrating, save the action schema, authentication method, and non-secret connection settings from the GPT editor's [Actions section](https://help.openai.com/en/articles/9442513-configuring-actions-in-gpts). Use these to fill gaps in the prompt, or ask the GPT owner for help.","usage_nature":"etapes","exemple":null,"verdict":"ignorer","date_ajout":"2026-10-16"},
{"id":"codex-mcp-2-connect-your-system","produit":"codex","categorie":"mcp","nom":"2. Connect your system","usage":"In the same conversation, ask Plugin Creator to connect the server to your system's API and walk you through sign-in. Use your organization's approved authentication method, and keep passwords, API keys, and other secrets out of chat.","usage_nature":"etapes","exemple":null,"verdict":"ignorer","date_ajout":"2026-10-16"},
{"id":"codex-mcp-3-create-a-new-sites-plugin","produit":"codex","categorie":"mcp","nom":"3. Create a new Sites plugin","usage":"$plugin-creator","usage_nature":"syntaxe","exemple":"$plugin-creator","verdict":"ignorer","date_ajout":"2026-10-16"},
{"id":"codex-mcp-3-publish-and-install","produit":"codex","categorie":"mcp","nom":"3. Publish and install","usage":"1. Open the plugin card, or find it under **Plugins → Personal → Created by you**.\n2. Follow **Install** and **Connect**, and complete any required sign-in.","usage_nature":"etapes","exemple":null,"verdict":"ignorer","date_ajout":"2026-10-16"},
{"id":"codex-mcp-4-use-your-plugin","produit":"codex","categorie":"mcp","nom":"4. Use your plugin","usage":"Start a new Work task, choose your plugin with **@**, and ask **“What's the status of ticket 123?”** using a ticket number from your system. You can use its tools alongside other plugins in the same conversation.","usage_nature":"etapes","exemple":null,"verdict":"ignorer","date_ajout":"2026-10-16"},
{"id":"codex-mcp-before-you-start","produit":"codex","categorie":"mcp","nom":"Before you start","usage":"Check the [Plugins directory](https://chatgpt.com/plugins) first. If you need a new connection, gather your system's API documentation and an approved way to connect. Ask the system owner if you need help.","usage_nature":"etapes","exemple":null,"verdict":"ignorer","date_ajout":"2026-10-16"},
{"id":"codex-mcp-build-an-mcp-plugin-with-plugin-creator-and-sites","produit":"codex","categorie":"mcp","nom":"Build an MCP plugin with Plugin Creator and Sites","usage":"Create a Support Ticket Lookup plugin with an MCP server hosted on Sites, using the attached [ticketing system] API docs. Let me look up a ticket's status, owner, and latest update by ticket number. Make it read-only and tell me what's needed to connect it.","usage_nature":"syntaxe","exemple":"Create a Support Ticket Lookup plugin with an MCP server hosted on Sites, using the attached [ticketing system] API docs. Let me look up a ticket's status, owner, and latest update by ticket number. Make it read-only and tell me what's needed to connect it.","verdict":"ignorer","date_ajout":"2026-10-16"},
{"id":"codex-mcp-connect-an-existing-mcp-server","produit":"codex","categorie":"mcp","nom":"Connect an existing MCP server","usage":"ChatGPT web uses remote MCP tools through plugins. If you already have a server, follow [Connect and test your plugin](https://developers.openai.com/plugins/deploy/connect-chatgpt). Local Codex clients can also connect directly to MCP servers and share their configuration.","usage_nature":"etapes","exemple":null,"verdict":"ignorer","date_ajout":"2026-10-16"},
{"id":"codex-mcp-replacing-a-gpt-custom-action","produit":"codex","categorie":"mcp","nom":"Replacing a GPT custom action","usage":"Write a prompt for ChatGPT Work or Codex to rebuild this workflow as MCP tools. Identify which operations read information and which make changes.\n\nInclude the API operation, inputs, returned fields, and answer format. Mark anything you don't know. Leave out credentials, secrets, and hidden instructions.\n\nAsk the builder to reuse the API and explain the connection setup.","usage_nature":"syntaxe","exemple":"Write a prompt for ChatGPT Work or Codex to rebuild this workflow as MCP tools. Identify which operations read information and which make changes.\n\nInclude the API operation, inputs, returned fields, and answer format. Mark anything you don't know. Leave out credentials, secrets, and hidden instructions.\n\nAsk the builder to reuse the API and explain the connection setup.","verdict":"ignorer","date_ajout":"2026-10-16"},
{"id":"codex-mcp-troubleshooting","produit":"codex","categorie":"mcp","nom":"Troubleshooting","usage":"For a connection error or missing tools, check that the Site owner published the latest version and that the plugin is installed and connected. Share any error with Plugin Creator or the server owner.","usage_nature":"etapes","exemple":null,"verdict":"ignorer","date_ajout":"2026-10-16"},
